{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"8c781aeb-ec03-47b4-9435-3aa571540f1e","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the MCP server and how it works. Let me also read the rest of `sequence_builder.py` to understand the `_set_step_properties` method and how properties are set on steps.\n\nNow let me plan the creation:\n\nThe xlsx file has test steps. Each step has:\n- Step_No (step number)\n- Step (startup/main - determines the step group)\n- Test project items (step name)\n- step type (PassFailTest, Action, NI_Flow_If, NI_Flow_Else, NI_Flow_End, NI_Wait, NumericLimitTest, SequenceCall)\n- instrument_vi (VI module path)\n- limits (like \"4.50<=x<=5.50\", \"x==0xaa\")\n- unit\n- format\n- run mode\n- wait(s)  \n- adapter\n- additional results\n- settings\n- Comment\n\nI need to create the sequence file step by step using the MCP tools. Let me create a comprehensive Python script that does this through an automated approach, since there are many steps.\n\nActually, looking at the available MCP tools more carefully:\n- `ts_create_sequence_file` - creates a new .seq file\n- `ts_add_step` - generic step with step_type, name, adapter, properties\n- `ts_add_wait` - wait step\n- `ts_add_numeric_limit_test` - numeric limit test with name, low, high\n- `ts_add_action` - action step with name, adapter, module_path\n- `ts_add_sequence` - add new subsequence\n- `ts_add_sequence_call` - call a subsequence\n- `ts_set_step_group` - set step group (setup/main/cleanup)\n- `ts_use_sequence` - switch to different sequence\n- `ts_save_sequence_file` - save\n\nFor the Excel data, I need to map the data to the appropriate MCP calls. Let me think about what properties need to be set for each step:\n\n1. **PassFailTest** with VI module:\n   - Step type: `PassFailTest`\n   - Adapter: from excel (col 10)\n   - Module path: from excel (col 4) - instrument_vi\n   - Additional results: from excel (col